---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';
---

<Base title={`About · ${profile.name}`}>
  <main class="page">
    <a class="back" href="/">&larr; home</a>

    <header class="head">
      <img class="portrait" src="/portrait.jpg" alt={`Portrait of ${profile.name}`} width="72" height="72" />
      <div>
        <p class="label">About</p>
        <h1 class="name">{profile.name}</h1>
      </div>
    </header>

    <p class="intro">
      I'm a researcher who became a builder. Over more than a decade building and scaling
      machine learning systems, one idea kept getting stronger: the most powerful AI should
      run on hardware you own. Your documents, your voice, your models, all on your machine,
      with nothing leaving it.
    </p>
    <p class="intro">
      That bet runs through everything I make. <a href="https://github.com/PromtEngineer/localGPT">localGPT</a>
      was an early proof that a private, fully offline retrieval system could actually be good.
      <a href="https://whryte.com">whryte</a> is the same idea for voice, transcription that never
      sends your audio anywhere. The wager doesn't change: you shouldn't have to hand your data to
      a server to use frontier-grade AI.
    </p>
    <p class="intro">
      I came to this through research. I earned a PhD in applied machine learning, working on
      wearable sensors and biomedical signal processing, problems where the data is about your own
      body and keeping it on-device isn't a preference but a requirement. That work led to a patent
      and a decade of published research, and the path from there runs through retrieval-augmented
      generation to the agentic systems I build today.
    </p>
    <p class="intro">
      These days I help companies build agentic systems and grow with them, as a consultant and an
      advisor, and I'm always chasing new things these systems can do. I share what I learn on my
      YouTube channel, <a href={profile.links.youtube}>Prompt Engineering</a>, where a community of
      engineers follows along.
    </p>

    <p class="proof-kicker">the record</p>
    <ul class="proof">
      <li><span class="k">PhD</span> applied machine learning</li>
      <li>
        <a href={profile.links.scholar}><span class="k">2,154</span> citations, h-index 21</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/PromtEngineer/localGPT"><span class="k">22,000&#9733;</span> localGPT on GitHub</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={profile.links.youtube}><span class="k">200,000</span> subscribers on YouTube</a>
      </li>
      <li><span class="k">Google Developer Expert</span>, AI/ML</li>
      <li><span class="k">Google Cloud NEXT 2025</span> speaker</li>
    </ul>

    <nav class="links" aria-label="Continue">
      <a class="more" href="/writing">Writing<span class="arrow">&nbsp;&rarr;</span></a>
      <a class="more" href={`mailto:${profile.email}?subject=AI%20consulting`}>AI consulting<span class="arrow">&nbsp;&rarr;</span></a>
    </nav>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    min-height: 100vh;
    min-height: 100svh;
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
    padding: 3rem clamp(1.5rem, 6vw, 4rem) 5rem;
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .back {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .back:hover,
  .back:focus-visible {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.1rem;
    margin: 3rem 0 2.2rem;
  }

  .portrait {
    width: 72px;
    height: 72px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgba(110, 103, 94, 0.5);
  }

  .label {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.28em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
  }

  .name {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 480;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .intro {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
    max-width: 38rem;
  }

  .intro a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-color: var(--rule-ink);
    transition: text-decoration-color 0.25s ease;
  }

  .intro a:hover,
  .intro a:focus-visible {
    text-decoration-color: var(--ink);
  }

  /* ——— the record ——— */

  .proof-kicker {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 3rem 0 1rem;
  }

  .proof {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1.5rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-ink);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-ink);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem 2.5rem;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .proof li {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .proof .k {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .proof a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .proof a:hover .k,
  .proof a:focus-visible .k {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .proof {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.85rem;
    }
  }

  /* ——— continue ——— */

  .links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.8rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .more {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 0.3s ease;
  }

  .more:hover,
  .more:focus-visible {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .arrow {
    display: inline-block;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease;
  }

  .more:hover .arrow,
  .more:focus-visible .arrow {
    transform: translateX(4px);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .arrow,
    .more {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
